        "thought_text": "Thought-2: To detect self-intersections efficiently, we need to consider the properties of the semi-circles. Specifically, we should check if the semi-circle formed by connecting the current point with the previous point intersects with any previously formed semi-circle. This involves comparing the y-coordinates of the intersection points of the semi-circles. We can use the formula for the intersection of two circles to determine if they intersect. However, since we are dealing with semi-circles, we need to adjust our approach to account for the fact that only the upper half of each circle is considered. A more efficient method might involve sorting the points by their x-coordinates and using a sweep line algorithm to detect intersections as we process each point. This would allow us to handle larger inputs more effectively.",
